  ai_summary: "A significant majority of patients are comfortable with artificial intelligence assisting in mammogram interpretation, provided a radiologist retains oversight, suggesting a positive trajectory for AI integration in breast cancer screening."
  
  Title: Apprenticeships to help ease shortage of radiologic technologists - Medical University of South Carolina
  Source: Google News Radiology
  URL: https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxQZl94bVk4UDVMX244UVh0OWdBeGQwbDh3NmVBcGFsa2F1Vm1sam1oeVM0QVJtWGFpVWhpQ3MtZTdveU81aTZpOVJZdmV5TVQ0N01ZTXBYMEo2cnd...s that a hidden mismatch between two common blood tests could quietly signal serious trouble ahead. When results from creatinine and cystatin C—two markers used to assess kidney health—don’t line up, the risk of kidney failure, heart disease, and even death appears to rise sharply. Researchers found that this gap is especially common among hospitalized and older patients, and that relying on just one test may miss early warning signs."
  Category: news
  Importance: 85
  ai_summary: "The increasing shortage of radiologic technologists is being addressed through the implementation of apprenticeship programs, offering a practical pathway for individuals to enter the field and alleviate workforce pressures."
  
